{"title":"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a plane convex quadrilateral of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the sum of the lengths of two opposite\nsides and one diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Determine all the possible lengths of the other diagonal.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Label the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in such a way that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63fd63b2ac457d6adcc4056fcc761ee40966e45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + BD + DC = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"177\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> is a diagonal.\n</p><p>The area of the quadrilateral can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aafbeaccb08b062d970d04e7b913bf3f40e617e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD \\cdot ( d_1 + d_2 ) / 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44612d9d6ec37da7f4edd0f205d65cdac5954dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/117778db99ba8932dc35128d085c2619f4f690a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> are altitudes from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52d84acc28e1335f9eab12450024f953548c911.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1 \\leq AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9ab07a35b19fa60d1878d0101fe6ece0a8c4073f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2 \\leq DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />. Hence the area is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c8828e4b783f63cd12bf8f9491ce6ffaba40e649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD \\cdot ( AB + DC ) / 2 = BD(16-BD) / 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"313\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The quadratic function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e86b67929367f1b8a44a5ecdc8c96d88284d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x(16-x)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> has its maximum for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf5d650726be49af3a306c54a2fd7dd1d628b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and its value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c0b3093be41d46d451b887840b5ff96a133a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(8)=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The area of our quadrilateral is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e491294491036a473e5229c66217003aa9bd9946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=8$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />. Also, equality must hold in both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52d84acc28e1335f9eab12450024f953548c911.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1 \\leq AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9ab07a35b19fa60d1878d0101fe6ece0a8c4073f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2 \\leq DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />. Hence both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b7e5ec2db31e9aded4bb09881b42d1c439fce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> must be perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. And in any such case it is clear from the Pythagorean theorem that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16589b07635aacb94ed0e588e354f9127f8335a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 8\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the other diagonal has only one possible length: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516de0cfacab78f3bb00ab40cda3f3c1b555c13d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be the quadrilateral, and assume AB, DC are the two sides\nand BD the diagonal whose sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a1e326f0334b3d88ab43a935d2dee9d41b49c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />.  For ease of writing, denote\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd021bd888ebf4700fa698885de105bb69b9d764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = AB, y = CD, z = BD, \\alpha = \\angle ABD, \\beta = \\angle CDB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Then, the area of the quadrilateral is the sum of the areas of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a9bb7efce753045eaf7bff4d2971daf83e427b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD, \\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />.  These are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676373a826f730d9bf33733ad7a93ea52f9609c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{area}\\ (\\triangle ABD) = \\frac{1}{2} xz \\sin \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df2457f11768f8331c764284ac6dd4c8ec06d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{area}\\ (\\triangle BCD) = \\frac{1}{2} yz \\sin \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Prob_1976_1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ad/Prob_1976_1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"397\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>The problem tells us that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a76a0fc175edfd116653188672a91cf80fb84cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + z = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261c34df123c7b931b8c2937fc9806edec007884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz \\sin \\alpha + yz \\sin \\beta = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/39826eaf94153001e9e665dc421b46b0d4839a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha, \\sin \\beta \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d8be6b2b134d522d9b421c29cf108630c235d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 16 - z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57cb25d00aa67b056573e97171fcb1c4eff69671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 = z (x \\sin \\alpha + y \\sin \\beta) \\le z (x + y) = z (16 - z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"377\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffcf3cb05514bd2a88941e48606aff8bd83d82b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2 - 16 z + 64 = (z - 8)^2 \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" />, so we must have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e528fd4b033f47f42fc258c8da96de3446a3a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.  Then we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c93b6cc7c49b57b6c5687eb3fd54664cc4048e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The two conditions of the problem become\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c93b6cc7c49b57b6c5687eb3fd54664cc4048e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f270c7cab8d040395927ed8004f324f6bdb29b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\sin \\alpha + y \\sin \\beta = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6eb4bc79b5ba963f8e4ea03f388f343ad6b8c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x (1 - \\sin \\alpha) + y (1 - \\sin \\beta) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"20\" />.\nSince both terms are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9c151a661a687f6e3e9b6e95ff672c231b6ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />, they must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b565bac841d29314d934b740199c912610ca47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha = \\sin \\beta = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1990e5a7eca886243ad6245157ce4173deae5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\beta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Now, look at the figure on the right.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> equals the sum of the\nhypotenuses of two isosceles right triangles with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/9805ddc58d4d6b6bd90cad6252d756923e6402b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = x \\sqrt{2} + y \\sqrt{2} = 8 \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"23\" />, which\nis the answer to the problem.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, December 2025]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO\" title=\"1976 IMO\">1976 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017054248\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 301/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9761/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.646      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.646      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4903:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017054248 and revision id 272862. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}